{"title": "Supreme Court: Voter List Deletion Doesn't Automatically Mean Citizenship Loss", "summary": "The Supreme Court has stated that deletion from electoral rolls does not automatically result in the loss of citizenship. While the court observed this, it did not issue a directive preventing the government from potentially impacting civil rights. The Election Commission can remove names from voter lists, but the ultimate authority on citizenship lies elsewhere.", "summary_points": ["Supreme Court observed that removal from voter lists does not equate to loss of citizenship.", "The court noted that the Election Commission has the power to delete voters' names.", "However, the Supreme Court did not issue a directive to the government regarding civil rights.", "The ultimate decision on citizenship is not determined by electoral roll status."], "title_hi": "सुप्रीम कोर्ट: मतदाता सूची से नाम हटने का मतलब नागरिकता का नुकसान नहीं", "summary_hi": "सुप्रीम कोर्ट ने कहा है कि मतदाता सूची से नाम हटाए जाने का मतलब स्वचालित रूप से नागरिकता का नुकसान नहीं है। हालांकि अदालत ने यह टिप्पणी की, लेकिन उसने सरकार को नागरिक अधिकारों को बाधित न करने का कोई निर्देश जारी नहीं किया। चुनाव आयोग मतदाताओं के नाम हटा सकता है, लेकिन नागरिकता पर अंतिम अधिकार कहीं और है।", "summary_points_hi": ["सुप्रीम कोर्ट ने कहा कि मतदाता सूची से नाम हटने का मतलब नागरिकता का नुकसान नहीं है।", "अदालत ने कहा कि चुनाव आयोग के पास मतदाताओं के नाम हटाने की शक्ति है।", "हालांकि, सुप्रीम कोर्ट ने सरकार को नागरिक अधिकारों के संबंध में कोई निर्देश जारी नहीं किया।", "नागरिकता का अंतिम निर्णय मतदाता सूची की स्थिति से निर्धारित नहीं होता है।"], "framing": {"left": ["Left-leaning outlets emphasize the Supreme Court's observation that voter list deletion does not mean loss of citizenship, while also noting the absence of a government directive on civil rights."]}, "framing_hi": {"left": ["वाम-झुकाव वाले आउटलेट सुप्रीम कोर्ट के इस अवलोकन पर जोर देते हैं कि मतदाता सूची से नाम हटने का मतलब नागरिकता का नुकसान नहीं है, साथ ही नागरिक अधिकारों पर सरकारी निर्देश की अनुपस्थिति को भी नोट करते हैं।"]}, "topic": "Crime & Law", "region": "India", "published_at": null, "image_url": "", "sources": [{"source": "The Wire", "owner": "The Wire", "lean": "left", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "SIR Deletion Wont Lead to Citizenship Loss, Repeats Supreme Court, But Doesnt Direct Govts to Not Hamper Civil Rights"}, {"source": "Scroll.in", "owner": "Scroll.in", "lean": "left", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "SIR: Exclusion from voter list does not mean loss of citizenship, observes Supreme Court"}, {"source": "The News Minute", "owner": "The News Minute", "lean": "left", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "SC says Election Commission can delete voters, but cannot decide citizenship"}, {"source": "LiveLaw", "owner": "LiveLaw", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMi-?oc=5", "headline": "SIR | Removal From Electoral Roll Doesn't Mean Loss Of Citizenship : Supreme Court"}, {"source": "LiveLaw", "owner": "LiveLaw", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "Art. 226 | High Courts Cannot Reweigh Evidence Or Interfere With Factual Findings In Certiorari..."}, {"source": "LiveLaw", "owner": "LiveLaw", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "Civil Court Can Examine Territorial Jurisdiction Afresh Even If High Court Granted Leave Before Suit..."}, {"source": "LiveLaw", "owner": "LiveLaw", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "Know The Law| When Can A Right Be Waived? Supreme Court Explains"}, {"source": "LiveLaw", "owner": "LiveLaw", "lean": "center", "language": "en", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5", "headline": "Know The Law | When Can High Courts Grant Relief Under Article 226 Beyond Pleadings? Supreme Court..."}, {"source": "The P